mailbox.resource/MB_GetCommandLine           mailbox.resource/MB_GetCommandLine

   NAME
	MB_GetCommandLine -- read the firmware's boot command line (V1.1)

   SYNOPSIS
	length = MB_GetCommandLine( reply, reply_capacity )
	d0                          a0     d0

	ULONG MB_GetCommandLine(STRPTR, ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Reads the ATAG/devicetree bootargs string the firmware handed to
	the kernel, using property tag GET_COMMAND_LINE (0x00050001).

   INPUTS
	reply           A buffer to receive the string, or NULL to discard it.
	reply_capacity  The size in bytes of the reply buffer. The reply is
	                truncated to whichever is smaller: this value or 1024.

   RESULTS
	length          The actual response length reported by the firmware,
	                or -1 on a mailbox transport error.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/dos.h>
	#include <proto/mailbox.h>
	#include <resources/mailbox.h>

	APTR MailboxBase = OpenResource(MAILBOXNAME);
	if (MailboxBase)
	{
	    UBYTE cmdline[256];

	    MB_GetCommandLine(cmdline, sizeof(cmdline));
	    Printf("Boot args: %s\n", cmdline);
	}

   SEE ALSO
	mailbox.resource/MB_StringCommand()

