mailbox.resource/MB_GetPhysicalSize         mailbox.resource/MB_GetPhysicalSize

   NAME
	MB_GetPhysicalSize -- read the framebuffer physical (display) size (V1.1)

   SYNOPSIS
	MB_GetPhysicalSize( width, height )
	                    a0     a1

	VOID MB_GetPhysicalSize(ULONG *, ULONG *);

   FUNCTION
	Reads the framebuffer's physical (visible display) size in
	pixels, using property tag GET_PHYSICAL_SIZE (0x00040003).

   INPUTS
	width           Receives the width in pixels, or NULL to discard.
	height          Receives the height in pixels, or NULL to discard.

   RESULTS
	On error, both *width and *height are set to -1.

   EXAMPLES
	Print both physical display sizes of a Raspberry Pi 4B, by
	selecting each display first with MB_SetDisplayNum() (BCM2711-only,
	see its own NOTE):

	    #include <exec/types.h>
	    #include <proto/exec.h>
	    #include <proto/dos.h>
	    #include <proto/mailbox.h>
	    #include <resources/mailbox.h>

	    extern APTR MailboxBase;

	    VOID PrintBothDisplaySizes(VOID)
	    {
	        ULONG display, width, height;

	        for (display = 0; display < 2; display++)
	        {
	            MB_SetDisplayNum(display);
	            MB_GetPhysicalSize(&width, &height);

	            Printf("HDMI%ld: %ld x %ld
	", display, width, height);
	        }
	    }

   SEE ALSO
	mailbox.resource/MB_SetPhysicalSize(),
	mailbox.resource/MB_GetVirtualSize(),
	mailbox.resource/MB_SetDisplayNum()

