	                16, 24, 32).

   RESULTS
	depth           The depth actually applied, or -1 on a mailbox
	                transport error.

   EXAMPLES
	#include <proto/exec.h>
	#include <proto/dos.h>
	#include <proto/mailbox.h>
	#include <resources/mailbox.h>

	APTR MailboxBase = OpenResource(MAILBOXNAME);
	if (MailboxBase)
	{
	    ULONG depth = MB_SetDepth(16);
	    Printf("Depth set to: %ld bpp\n", depth);
	}

   SEE ALSO
	mailbox.resource/MB_GetDepth(),
	mailbox.resource/MB_AllocateBuffer(),
	mailbox.resource/MB_SetDisplayNum()

mailbox.resource/MB_SetDisplayNum             mailbox.resource/MB_SetDisplayNum

   NAME
	MB_SetDisplayNum -- select the target display for framebuffer tags (V1.1)

   SYNOPSIS
	display_num = MB_SetDisplayNum( display_num )
	d0                              d0

	ULONG MB_SetDisplayNum(ULONG);

   FUNCTION
	Selects which physical display (0=HDMI0, 1=HDMI1) the
	framebuffer property tags that follow --
	MB_GetPhysicalSize/MB_SetPhysicalSize,
	MB_GetVirtualSize/MB_SetVirtualSize, MB_GetDepth/MB_SetDepth,
	MB_GetPitch, MB_AllocateBuffer, MB_ReleaseBuffer, MB_BlankScreen
	and friends -- apply to, using property tag SET_DISPLAY_NUM
	(0x00048013). BCM2711-only (Raspberry Pi 4 family); has no
	effect on earlier SoCs, which only ever had one HDMI output.

   INPUTS
	display_num     0 for HDMI0, 1 for HDMI1.

   RESULTS
	display_num     The display number actually selected, or -1 on a
	                mailbox transport error.

   EXAMPLES
	Print both physical display sizes of a Raspberry Pi 4B,
	checking that each display selection succeeds before querying it
	(see MB_GetPhysicalSize() for the full loop):

	    #include <exec/types.h>
	    #include <proto/exec.h>
	    #include <proto/dos.h>
	    #include <proto/mailbox.h>
	    #include <resources/mailbox.h>

	    extern APTR MailboxBase;

	    ULONG display = 1; /* HDMI1 */

	    if (MB_SetDisplayNum(display) == display)
	    {
	        ULONG width, height;

	        MB_GetPhysicalSize(&width, &height);
	        Printf("HDMI%ld: %ld x %ld
	", display, width, height);
	    }
	    else
	    {
	        Printf("HDMI%ld: not available
	", display);
	    }

   NOTE
	This tag is not documented in Michal Schulz's canonical
	resources/mailbox.h; its existence and behaviour come from
	third-party bare-metal reports and have not yet been verified on
	this project's own hardware.

   SEE ALSO
	mailbox.resource/MB_GetPhysicalSize(),
	mailbox.resource/MB_AllocateBuffer()

